        "id": 1186019
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-03-14T01:47:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, these registers need to be protected by safe mode. those are for supper-speed lines.\nUSB Type-C Specification Release 1.2: \"The USB Safe State is defined by the USB PD specification. The USB Safe State defines an electrical state for the SBU1/2 and SSTX/SSRX for DFPs, UFPs, and Active Cables when transitioning between USB and an Alternate Mode. SBU1/2 and SSTX/SSRX must transition to the USB Safe State before entering to or exiting from an Alternate Mode.\"",
      "parentUuid": "fd2091e7_7a2c4dba",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 167,
        "startChar": 22,
        "endLine": 167,
        "endChar": 47
      },
      "revId": "8e009573c47e482953edc64961cd7852ed57d3be",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
